# Clientbound `minecraft:custom_payload` packet BODY (everything after the
# packet id) carrying a `minecraft:brand` payload from an unmodified server.
#
# PROVENANCE. Hand-derived from the 26.2 wire specification, matching the
# convention `crates/versions/26.2/tests/clientbound_backlog.rs:9-12` states for
# this exact packet ("Golden byte vectors are hand-built from the wire
# specification (26.2 decompiled Mojang source), not round-tripped through this
# crate's own encoder, so a self-consistent misreading cannot pass silently").
# It is deliberately NOT produced by `lodestone_v26_2`'s own encoder, and no test
# in this crate encodes anything — so `decode(encode(x)) == x` cannot be what
# makes the gate pass.
#
# LAYOUT. `ClientboundCustomPayloadPacket` is a channel identifier then the
# channel's payload occupying the rest of the frame. `BrandPayload` is a single
# `FriendlyByteBuf::readUtf`. Both strings are VarInt byte-length then UTF-8:
#
#   0f                                  VarInt 15 -- length of the channel name
#   6d 69 6e 65 63 72 61 66 74 3a       "minecraft:"
#   62 72 61 6e 64                      "brand"
#   07                                  VarInt 7 -- length of the brand string
#   76 61 6e 69 6c 6c 61                "vanilla"
#
# 24 bytes total. `#` comments and all whitespace are ignored by the loader.

0f 6d 69 6e 65 63 72 61 66 74 3a 62 72 61 6e 64
07 76 61 6e 69 6c 6c 61
